---
description: Keep three concurrent agents from editing the same work
alwaysApply: true
---

# Concurrent lanes

- Work product code only on your lane branch: `lane/1`, `lane/2`, or `lane/3`.
- One person per lane, recorded in `docs/STATUS.md`. Do not edit another lane's row.
- `main` is protected: nothing is pushed to it directly. Docs and claims go through a `ctx/lane-N-<topic>` PR with `gh pr merge --auto --merge`; code goes through a `lane/N` PR. Both need the `build` check green.
- Claim files in `docs/STATUS.md` via a `ctx/...` PR, wait for it to merge, then code. Full steps: `docs/COORDINATION.md`.
- Do not edit files an `active` claim already lists.
- Do not force-push `main` or another person's branch.
- Before you stop, set your claim to `idle` or `blocked` and write a one-line handoff.
